nal geostrophy, referenced to1500dbar. The selected path is not a fixed-depth, absolute-current or observed velocity-core axis.\",\"note\":\"Western mean-circulation reference reach between OSW offshore gates164E and180E. Gates and bends are editorial, not physical origin/termination or source-extracted axis points. Excludes upstream island branches, eastern seasonal extensions, SEC return, STCC and subsurface equatorial jets. No whole-current length.\",\"observation_date\":null,\"physical_current_axis_admitted\":false,\"physical_state_join_eligible\":false,\"role\":\"editorial_reference_route\",\"source_file_sha256\":\"a8bb517551f04dbe1018a6d5a51817cee4c3e3afaf2d82447bccdab03cef1d85\",\"source_id\":\"source:chen-qiu-secc-seasonal-2004\",\"source_locator\":\"Paragraph2 on PDF page1 and Figure1b/caption on PDF page2: western SECC context and mean0-200m geostrophy relative to1500dbar. Selected page2 pixels actually reviewed on2026-10-27.\",\"source_url\":\"https://www.soest.hawaii.edu/oceanography/bo/CQ04.pdf\",\"time_convention\":\"WOA01 mean-field context only. Publication2004 is not an observation date. No dated trajectory or seasonal route reconstructed.\"}],\"measurement_ids\":[],\"nasa_links\":1,\"object_url\":\"object.html?id=current%3Apacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\"published_length_km\":null,\"recorded_claims\":56,\"route_decision_ids\":[\"route-decision:pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent\"],\"route_ids\":[\"pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent-western-mean-reference-reach-v1\"],\"route_url\":\"reference-routes.html?atlas-layout=map&atlas-feature=current%3Apacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent&atlas-route=pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent-western-mean-reference-reach-v1#route-atlas\",\"scope_notes\":[{\"audit_file\":\"research/pacific-secc-argo-seasonal-extent-scope-audit.json\",\"current_id\":\"pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\"label\":\"Argo seasonal envelope and dateline scope\",\"observed_period\":null,\"source_locator\":\"Publisher abstract, Plain Language Summary and Data Availability Statement.\",\"source_url\":\"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2025JC023053?af=R\",\"summary\":\"Source preview reports a spring envelope from 150 E to 170 W and an autumn extension to 140 W. These dateline-crossing spans are not traced current lengths. Spring latitude limits are not paired current edges; full methods, averaging years and calendar months remain unresolved.\"},{\"audit_file\":\"research/pacific-secc-woa01-anomaly-scope-audit.json\",\"current_id\":\"pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\"label\":\"WOA01 mean flow and seasonal anomaly separation\",\"observed_period\":null,\"source_locator\":\"Figures 1, 2 and 8; paragraphs 2-3, 20 and 26.\",\"source_url\":\"https://www.soest.hawaii.edu/oceanography/bo/CQ04.pdf\",\"summary\":\"Full 2004 paper distinguishes surface and 0-200 m WOA01 geostrophy relative to 1500 dbar, modeled Sverdrup flow, and band-passed seasonal anomaly sections at 170 E. Anomaly zero contours and averaging windows cannot define current widths or endpoints. Numerical compatible flow fields remain needed.\"}],\"season_url\":\"seasons.html?current=pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\"section_fingerprints\":{\"claims\":\"a2260e85e85cdaacd05696a2bbc881fb6f1e636ebc87bed5300f637bf643449c\",\"identity\":\"0a7c9e3aeadc47415d4d10a028f9175f4ae733f8e295ba3a97a4b47de019c4a4\",\"measurements\":\"48898dff5dc1c51f0d87ec135947e45563dfef5209883cd906076bda24075e23\",\"media\":\"68658cd0ec2f73124154cc258620ecc3b963fde1f88b1db76b5ddb15420c2128\",\"pacific_secc_western_reference\":\"de110b943b30e095c0ff37a17859c4eb3f665aae90e6e89ff9fa91da71cc989e\",\"routes_geometry\":\"74aeb995dc693bc0f23130b0cba8251d723d2686090deea7764749eca886698f\",\"sources\":\"fc499f8708a71982e37552a03408341daeae9bce690af22335d5fd8aadbcac63\",\"time_evidence\":\"8d86da8229951992c802d517eaeaeeb84a4b5f1a3e916ecd7944f448135387bd\"},\"series\":[],\"setting\":\"equatorial\",\"source_ids\":