h calculation.","Separate ENSO composites from seasonal climatology and justify named-flow endpoints.","Independent scientific and canonical admission review."],"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Reported seasonal geographic envelopes from Argo-derived absolute geostrophic currents; not a measured current axis or velocity-boundary width.","seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"source_access":"Publisher preview inspected. Full methods, figures and supplementary file not acquired; study averaging years and calendar-month definitions unresolved.","source_citation":"Wu, Yang and Liang (2026), Seasonal and Interannual Variability of the Pacific South Equatorial Countercurrent Based on Argo Profiles, doi:10.1029/2025JC023053.","source_locator":"Publisher abstract, Plain Language Summary and Data Availability Statement.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-04","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2025JC023053?af=R","status":"editorial_source_scope_not_scientific_approval","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null},"note":{"audit_file":"research/pacific-secc-argo-seasonal-extent-scope-audit.json","current_id":"pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Argo seasonal envelope and dateline scope","observed_period":null,"source_locator":"Publisher abstract, Plain Language Summary and Data Availability Statement.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2025JC023053?af=R","summary":"Source preview reports a spring envelope from 150 E to 170 W and an autumn extension to 140 W. These dateline-crossing spans are not traced current lengths. Spring latitude limits are not paired current edges; full methods, averaging years and calendar months remain unresolved."},"source_sha256":"09cd0ecd3e76bdb88266cd8543c87b55465cc9015446b32ae2330cbd85fe2995"},{"document":{"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"current_id":"pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent","field_suppor