ranch":"altimetric SSH anomaly","paired_velocity_boundary_coordinates_lon_lat":null,"quantity":"seasonal_zonal_geostrophic_velocity_from_band_passed_ssh","source_locator":"Paragraphs 20 and 26; Figure 8","source_sign_encoding":"Negative anomalies shaded; velocity contours in cm/s.","width_extraction_admissible":false}],"geographic_rule":"Reference pressure is not current-axis depth. Geographic/averaging windows are not paired edges. Model boundaries and zero velocity-anomaly contours do not establish total-flow boundaries; do not add the WOA01 mean to the differently referenced altimetric anomaly field without reviewed compatibility.","historical_comparison":{"comparability":"Different longitudes, layers, periods and methods; seasonal signs cannot be pooled into a uniform named-current calendar.","source_locator":"Paragraph 3; summaries of Gouriou and Toole (1993) and Reverdin et al. (1994)","underlying_originals_inspected":false},"mean_geographic_context":{"reported_latitude_band_degrees":[-11,-8],"role":"regional_context_not_paired_velocity_edges","source_locator":"Paragraph 2"},"observed_period":null,"remaining_gates":["Acquire compatible numerical mean/monthly velocity fields and resolve their reference state, averaging periods and uncertainty.","Recover longitudinal connected velocity-core support and source-defined gates before tracing a route; do not bridge separated positive components.","Use paired total-flow boundaries for local width extraction; anomaly zero crossings remain inadmissible as current-width edges.","Keep 2004 relative-geostrophic support separate from the 2026 Argo absolute-geostrophic envelopes and ENSO composites.","Independent scientific boundary, identity and canonical admission review."],"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","scope":"Keep mean relative geostrophy, modeled flow and seasonal anomaly sections distinct before route or width extraction.","seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"source_access":"University-hosted full