"name\": \"South Indian Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n      \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n      \"scope\": \"Declared 70 E to 90 E eastern-name-convention regional reach. The west gate follows the later convention reserving South Indian Ocean Current for flow beyond the Agulhas Return Current near 70 E; the east gate is the approximate recirculation/splitting region described in historical hydrography. These are selected regional gates, not whole-current endpoints. Western Agulhas Return, northward recirculation, northeastern Australia continuation and ACC paths are not added. All route latitudes and connecting vertices are editorial.\",\r\n      \"route_extent_kind\": \"eastern regional reach\",\r\n      \"approximate_reference_path_km\": 1700,\r\n      \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n        1600,\r\n        1800\r\n      ],\r\n      \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1029/96JC03455\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997), section 3.2 / journal p. 5523 and Figure 7 caption: 90 E recirculation/split and upper-1000 m flow schematic. Later Grand et al. (2015), regional circulation discussion, journal p. 113: SIOC name beyond 70 E. Near-40 S context from Stramma (1992) publisher abstract; drawn latitudes are editorial.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://journals.ametsoc.org/abstract/journals/phoc/22/4/1520-0485_1992_022_0421_tsioc_2_0_co_2.xml\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Stramma (1992), The South Indian Ocean Current, JPO 22, 421–430.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Publisher abstract only: near-40 S STF context and eastern separation beyond 100 E.\",\r\n          \"supports\": \"Broad earlier current name and approximate frontal geography; no source centerline digitized.\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924796301000410\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Lutjeharms and Ansorge (2001), The Agulhas Return Current, Journal of Marine Systems 30, 115–138.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct publisher retrieval returned 403.\",\r\n          \"supports\": \"Proposed ARC termination near 66–70 E and SIOC name farther east; source convention, not fixed physical junction.\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://science.whoi.edu/users/mcgillic/cruises/TN376/cruiseshare/Morton%20lab/Relevant%20Papers/Grand%20et%20al.%20-%202015%20-%20The%20impact%20of%20circulation%20and%20dust%20deposition%20in%20controlling%20the%20distributions%20of%20dissolved%20Fe%20and%20Al%20in%20the%20south.pdf\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Grand et al. (2015), The impact of circulation and dust deposition in controlling the distributions of dissolved Fe and Al in the south Indian subtropical gyre, Marine Chemistry 176, 110–125.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Regional circulation discussion, journal p. 113 / PDF page 4.\",\r\n          \"supports\": \"SIOC name beyond 70 E; near-90 E recirculation and dispersed eastern flow.\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"candidate_file\": \"research/south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"candidate_sha256\": \"5ffe93eddca3a110dedfc3a0d2dfb589504d60422e24729e0820629b4a94eafe\",\r\n      \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n      \"figure\": \"figures/south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\",\r\n      \"nominal_atlas_state_crossings\": [\r\n        \"ISSG\",\r\n        \"SANT\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_E_5\",\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Review the longitude naming transition and exact regional layer against compatible velocity fields.\",\r\n        \"Resolve the distinction among South Indian Current, South Indian Ocean Current and Agulhas Return under each source convention.\",\r\n        \"Diagnose meanders and local latitude shifts; the near-40 S editorial connection is not an observed axis.\",\r\n        \"Resolve the 90 E branching and northeastern continuation independently before any whole-current length.\",\r\n        \"Recover matching seasonal axes and transverse boundaries before annual length/width ranges.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"parent_current_id\": null,\r\n      \"parent_scope_note\": null,\r\n      \"ordering_sensitivity\": null\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"tasman-historical-connection-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"tasman-front\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Tasman Front\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n      \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n      \"scope\": \"Historical Tasman Front naming convention represented by an OSW offshore 154 E to 172 E near-34 S regional connection. Gates truncate the Australia-northern-New-Zealand geography; neither coastal endpoints nor a continuously identifiable jet is claimed. Excludes coastal EAC, southern extension and East Auckland coastal continuation.\",\r\n      \"route_extent_kind\": \"historical Tasman reference connection\",\r\n      \"approximate_reference_path_km\": 1700,\r\n      \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n        1600,\r\n        1800\r\n      ],\r\n      \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://ocg.aori.u-tokyo.ac.jp/member/eoka/documents/Tomczak_Godfrey.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Chapter 8, printed pp127-129 / PDF137-139: Australia-New Zealand connection near 34 S, meanders and statistically defined average position. Version 1.1 March 2005. Cited pages and Figure 8.23 visually inspected.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"label\": \"Oke et al. (2019), A search for the Tasman Front, doi:10.1016/j.jmarsys.2019.103217\",\r\n          \"url\"