group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n      \"scope\": \"Declared 103 W to 88 W eastern regional studied reach between two reported Subtropical Front crossings associated with the SPC in the source regional surface circulation. Front locations are proxies, not diagnosed velocity-core endpoints, and were observed in different years. OSW connecting vertices and alternatives are editorial. Branch correspondence is unresolved. Excludes Chatham Rise/western basin, ACC export branch, Peru-Chile coastal flow, northward recirculation and independent split bands. Not a whole-current or simultaneous observed axis.\",\r\n      \"route_extent_kind\": \"STF-proxy regional reach\",\r\n      \"approximate_reference_path_km\": 1400,\r\n      \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n        1300,\r\n        1500\r\n      ],\r\n      \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2024-12/010047303.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Data [4]–[5], surface circulation [7], STF [14]–[17] and Table 1: P18 at 103 W 33.8 S and P19 at 88 W 34.5 S. Source front/velocity distinction retained; fields and curves not digitized.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/phoc/25/1/1520-0485_1995_025_0077_tspc_2_0_co_2.xml\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Stramma, Peterson and Tomczak (1995), The South Pacific Current, JPO 25, 77–91.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct article/PDF access unsuccessful.\",\r\n          \"supports\": \"SPC distinction from ACC, broad Chatham Rise context and possible splitting at 115–85 W. Does not assign a branch to this connection.\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2007GL030392\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Ridgway and Dunn (2007), Observational evidence for a Southern Hemisphere oceanic supergyre, GRL