urface reference reach between observations at 35 W near 5 N and the central observational neighborhood at 23 W near 5 N. Connecting vertices are editorial, not an observed continuous axis. Excludes NBC/NEC source recirculation, surface NECC flow, uncertain filaments east of 28 W and farther-east termination. Not full-current source-to-end length.\",\r\n      \"route_extent_kind\": \"35 W–23 W subsurface reference reach\",\r\n      \"approximate_reference_path_km\": 1300,\r\n      \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n        1200,\r\n        1400\r\n      ],\r\n      \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Bourles et al. (1999), section 4.8, p. 21163: 35 W NEUC centered at 5 N in February 1993 and April 1996; core near sigma-theta 26.75. Sections 4.6 and 6.1 separate source retroflection from the named current; eastern filament context cites earlier work.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://pureadmin.uhi.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/14119479/2020GL088350.pdf\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt, Claus and Hahn (2020), Fluctuations of the Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent and Associated Changes in Oxygen Transports, GRL 47, e2020GL088350, doi:10.1029/2020GL088350.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Introduction and sections 2–4, pp. 1–4: central 5 N, 23 W observations and 65–270 m definition; data intervals and fixed-box/inferred-transport distinctions.\",\r\n          \"role\": \"Central observational context; weak seasonal cycle and episodic intraseasonal events do not establish seasonal geometry.\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014760\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt and Duteil (2019), Interannual Variability of the Atlantic North Equatorial Underc