gth.\",\r\n        \"Whole-current length, physical width and annual ranges remain unresolved.\",\r\n        \"No seasonal playback, occupied polygon, physical state containment or NASA current identity inferred.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"parent_current_id\": null,\r\n      \"parent_scope_note\": null,\r\n      \"ordering_sensitivity\": null\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"redsox-northern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"red-sea-saline-overflow\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Red Sea saline overflow - northern plume reference reach\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n      \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n      \"scope\": \"Declared northern descending-plume regional connection from an OSW Bab-el-Mandeb approach gate toward the Figure 1 lower-channel neighborhood. Every vertex is an independent rounded editorial choice. Excludes the other branch, gully products, late equilibrated-water spreading and a whole-parent length.\",\r\n      \"route_extent_kind\": \"northern descending-plume reference reach\",\r\n      \"approximate_reference_path_km\": 120,\r\n      \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n        110,\r\n        130\r\n      ],\r\n      \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www2.whoi.edu/site/bower-lab/wp-content/uploads/sites/12/2018/03/Peters_2005_MixingEntrainment.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Peters et al. (2005), section 2, section 3a and Figure 1 printed571 / PDF3 identify two preferred descending plume pathways. Section5a printed575 / PDF7 describes non-synoptic velocity-supported northern reach 130 km; channel lengths / 5 km width are different objects. Source figure inspected for orientation only.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [],\r\n      \"candidate_file\": \"research/redsox-northern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"candidate_sha256\": \"c5cbd42353d683815c523b611be5fd52f3f6639badc2ae9393c15