incem.unibo.it/images/reports/2011_Poulain_Aspects_of_the_surface_circulation.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Poulain et al. (2012), Introduction pp. 261–263: NC formation and Italian/French coastal continuation; sections 2.1 and 4, pp. 264–266 and 274–276: surface sampling, Genoa, Imperia, Menton–Nice and current structure.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=3357\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Marine Regions / VLIZ, MRGID 3357, Ligurian Current; ASFA thesaurus naming entry.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Place details: Proposed standard, Current, part of Mediterranean Sea; no current endpoint or length geometry supplied.\",\r\n          \"role\": \"Naming reference only; does not define this coastal reach or certify Northern Current segment boundaries.\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/689/2018/\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Berta et al. (2018), Wind-induced variability in the Northern Current (northwestern Mediterranean Sea) as depicted by a multi-platform observing system, Ocean Science 14, 689–710, doi:10.5194/os-14-689-2018.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Introduction: Liguro-Provencal-Catalan / Northern Current formed in Ligurian Sea and recognizable through Catalan Sea.\",\r\n          \"role\": \"Broader parent geography; whole-parent length and regional width summaries are not transferred to this segment.\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"candidate_file\": \"research/ligurian-reach-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"candidate_sha256\": \"097cef899d328b72f4069125e1f30d3d5663a9502ca500d74d0ccbeb318a0bba\",\r\n      \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n      \"figure\": \"figures/ligurian-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\",\r\n      \"nominal_atlas_state_crossings\": [\r\n        \"MEDI\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"recommended_nasa_