uct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Pacific North Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"Repeated Pacific velocity sections identify a near-surface eastward core around 7°N at 140°W. The section locates the current but gives no comparable along-current length.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"eastward upper-ocean countercurrent\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"expand_section_evidence\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Extend evidence beyond sections\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"Repeated Pacific velocity sections identify a near-surface eastward core around 7°N at 140°W. The section locates the current but gives no comparable along-current length.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Find sourced upstream/downstream gates and continuity between sections; preserve widths and section transports as different measurements.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Pacific North Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"section_only\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"The 130°E mooring array measures eastward subsurface jets between 8.5°N and 17.5°N, with 5.1 Sv mean positive transport to 900 m under the study definition. This cross-section is not a path length.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.979442/full\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"pacific-neuc-middle-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n        \"pacific-neuc-northern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n        \"pacific-neuc-southern-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"intermittent subsurface jets\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"layer_specific_route\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Construct layer-specific paths\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"The 130°E mooring array measures eastward subsurface jets between 8.5°N and 17.5°N, with 5.1 Sv mean positive transport to 900 m under the study definition. This cross-section is not a path length.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Pacific North Subsurface Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"A Pacific section at 140°W locates this eastward jet near 4°N and 200 m; the section does not determine its complete alongflow route or length.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"eastward subsurface jet north of the Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"layer_specific_route\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Construct layer-specific paths\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"A Pacific section at 140°W locates this eastward jet near 4°N and 200 m; the section does not determine its complete alongflow route or length.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Pacific South Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"Argo-based analysis reports a boreal-spring band near 5–13°S from 150°E to 170°W, with seasonal changes in zonal reach and depth. That observed seasonal envelope is not a traced alongstream length and is unranked.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/2025JC023053\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"reference_path_not_constructed\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"seasonally varying eastward countercurrent\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"seasonal_routes\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Construct seasonal routes\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"Argo-based analysis reports a boreal-spring band near 5–13°S from 150°E to 170°W, with seasonal changes in zonal reach and depth. That observed seasonal envelope is not a traced alongstream length and is unranked.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Recover compatible numerical total-flow axes and paired boundaries; keep WOA01 surface/0-200 m geostrophy relative to 1500 dbar separate from modeled Sverdrup flow and band-passed anomaly sections at 170 E. Do not use anomaly zero contours as width edges, averaging windows as endpoints, or merge them with the newer Argo envelopes. See research/pacific-secc-woa01-anomaly-scope-audit.json; full 2026 methods and seasonal calendars remain needed.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"pacific-south-subsurface-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Pacific South Subsurface Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"The Pacific 140°W section resolves two south-side branches near 4.5°S at 200 m and 7°S at 250 m. These section positions do not supply a whole-current path length or a single branch-averaged centerline.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"eastward subsurface jets south of the Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"layer_specific_route\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Construct layer-specific paths\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"The Pacific 140°W section resolves two south-side branches near 4.5°S at 200 m and 7°S at 250 m. These section positions do not supply a whole-current path length or a single branch-averaged centerline.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"persian-gulf-saline-overflow\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Persian Gulf saline overflow\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"NASA identifies a saline overflow contribution from the Persian Gulf to the western Indian Ocean. The Strait of Hormuz gateway is not a measured plume endpoint or a whole-flow centerline; dilution and circulation beyond the strait require sepa