es describe boundary-choice sensitivity, not confidence limits, temporal variation or annual extrema. Tube definitions cannot be averaged or added.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Section C northwest/north of Svalbard, August 2015; local WSC stream-tube support. C is upstream of branch partitioning; tube 2 constrains a Svalbard-branch interpretation.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Source cross-current survey section; no geographic edge pair or flow-normal projection extracted.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Property-defined Atlantic Water (practical salinity >34.88; corresponding rounded absolute salinity >35.05 g/kg; conservative temperature >=2 C), limited by seabed; not a fixed depth interval.\",\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Synoptic August 2015 cruise context, 12-21 August; exact section dates unextracted. Three sections span about five days, not seasonal phases.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Tube 1: first transport-density drop on either side of core below AW thickness times 0.04 m/s; C offshore edge x=-11 km from SADCP. Separate 0.02/0.08 m/s sensitivity cases.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1603/2018/\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Kolas, E. and Fer, I. (2018), Hydrography, transport and mixing of the West Spitsbergen Current: the Svalbard Branch in summer 2015, Ocean Science 14, 1603-1618, doi:10.5194/os-14-1603-2018.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Table 2, printed p.1611, Width (km), section C, stream tube 1; methods sections 3.2-3.3, pp.1606-1608.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-08\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_synoptic_section_diagnostic\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Transcribed original PDF Table 2 cells after rendering and visual inspection; numeric methods read. No new inversion or geographic edge digitization.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"wid