Western cold-water vein / separate thermal metric: 100–150 km, author trade-wind surface cold-water vein. This thermal metric is separate from current-anomaly width. No midpoint, annual extrema, mapped edges or numerical uncertainty supplied.\",\r\n        \"display_caption\": \"Western cold-water vein / separate thermal metric: 100–150 km. Trade-wind / austral-winter description, illustrated by August seasonal fields. Thermal water-mass span following the current core; separate from the velocity-anomaly vein.\",\r\n        \"display_method_note\": \"2001–2010 seasonal climatology context; exact width dates, paired edges and uncertainty unresolved. Current descriptors share one source claim and overlap geographically; the near-200 km western maxima are a subset of the 100–200 km western span. Figure 3 variability-envelope widths, 80/340 km SLA smoothing, core displacement and offshore core position remain distinct metrics. No seasonal width animation inferred.\",\r\n        \"quality_note\": \"Complete unchanged HAL deposit inspected. Author regional numbers retained with their metrics and seasonal context; paired boundaries and numeric errors not recovered.\",\r\n        \"source_pdf_sha256\": \"6da50667b80790752fa0189ff9cf0cdfd88c521509b0f393365de306286bacbe\",\r\n        \"protocol_file\": \"plans/ngcc-seasonal-vein-width-protocol-v1.md\",\r\n        \"protocol_sha256\": \"e39b24d49fea763f129e82e9c76dbaa6f2e23b6d5485ffb6e4008ee5b4038d73\",\r\n        \"boundary_coordinates_extracted\": false,\r\n        \"full_width_conversion_admitted\": false,\r\n        \"audit_file\": \"research/ngcc-radenac-2016-seasonal-vein-width-scope-audit.json\",\r\n        \"audit_sha256\": \"223405cce3aa4a5fecdf94dd25ebff225a9594f33fb04f784a469fd4e6e8ce10\",\r\n        \"audit_pointer\": \"/measurements/3\"\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"azores-carracedo-2014-spring-core-width\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"WOA09 spring climatology (April-June)\",\r\n      \"source_season_label\": \"spring\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": [\r\n        4,\r\n        5,\r\n        6\r\n      ],\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 240,\r\n      \"source_reported_maximum_core_depth_m\": 790,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"measurement_uncertainty_interval_km\": null,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"current_id\": \"azores\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Azores Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_regional_seasonal_summary\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_inverse_model_velocity_threshold_core_span\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"seasonal_summary\",\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Approximate source-reported seasonal core value; no width uncertainty interval supplied.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Western WOA-Box section at 19.5 W. A regional cross-current model core extent, with no paired edge coordinates extracted.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Meridional western WOA-Box section; no exact flow-normal correction inferred.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Depth-varying inverse-model section. Source reports maximum core depth about 790 m in spring and 1100 m in autumn; these are source-reported vertical context, not fixed depth layers at which these widths were measured.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"WOA09 mixed historical climatologies in a regional inverse model; source quarter WOA09 spring climatology (April-June). Not an individual occupation or dated current footprint.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Author defines the core using velocities greater than 2 cm/s. No full-current envelope or universal half-peak threshold inferred.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://nora.nerc.ac.uk/id/eprint/521101/1/1-s2.0-S0079661113002437-main.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Carracedo, Gilcoto, Mercier and Perez (2014), Seasonal dynamics in the Azores-Gibraltar Strait region: A